From f7b25b384883ab88be6c178e33333cb1b6e6fbca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:34:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-114: a page opens at the zoom it had last time --
 the defaultZoom setting, as WPF's "Default zoom setting" (0.114.0)

WPF (Tools > Options > XAML Designer) opens a document at the zoom it had last
(Last Used, the default) or fitting the view (Fit All). Here every page opened
at 100%. Now each page's zoom is kept in the workspace state (dropped when it
is back at 100%) and a page opens at it again. New setting
ht9045Designer.defaultZoom = last (the default) / fit (the first drawing fits the
view, a redraw keeps its zoom) / 100 (every time 100%, as before).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 190, panels, real VS Code 159):
smoke (last by default, nonsense = last; zoomed to 150% -> the page opened again
at 150%; fit -> the first init asks to fit, a redraw does not; back at 100% ->
nothing kept).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
